// "<spell or ability> resolves" [CR#608.1,608.2], Lean's `resolve`
// Definition: no player carries it out or pays for it, but an event names it.
// As the final part of an instant or sorcery spell's resolution the spell is
// put into its owner's graveyard [CR#608.2n], so "as it resolves" (buyback,
// rebound) and "during its resolution" (haunt) write the resolution as the
// cause of that move: `causes(Event(verbedEvent(resolve, thisSpell)), …)`. A
// countered spell's move is caused by no resolution [CR#701.6a].
KeywordAction(
    name: "resolve",
    params: [Subject],
    spelling: "resolve <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "resolve",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    body: procedure(Resolve, Param(0), ItsOwnCost),
)
